	'k05906393' => 'it arrives with sudden weakness, face droop, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life.',
	'k06be6ff1' => 'Hisagi Neurology is on the second floor of 14 Linden Row, Westmere. Tram line 4 stops at Linden Row, a two-minute walk from the door.',
	'k07149639' => 'HISAGI NEUROLOGY',
	'k07a14560' => '€180<br>first visit',
	'k07e3e742' => 'What to bring',
	'k0926b5d4' => 'THREE THINGS IN EVERY LETTER',
	'k09e85317' => 'Leila Haddad',
	'k0aac21a9' => 'You are not booked until we reply. Include the same four things: the symptom, the duration, the GP\'s name, and the medicines. The phone number is 010 482 0116, answered Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30, by the patient coordinator.',
	'k0b652458' => 'You sit with one doctor, in one room, for the full hour, from the first question through the examination by hand.',
	'k0ba3e831' => 'FOUNDED IN 2012',
	'k0c758181' => 'After ten weeks she said, in her own words, that she writes letters again. The before of this story is a cup held in both hands. The after is a pen on a kitchen table. Name and details are changed. This is one person\'s account, not a forecast for the next person through the door.',
	'k0d4382ab' => 'you have had an unexplained blackout, a possible seizure, or spells your GP wants a neurologist to hear.',
	'k0e0f44c5' => 'SEVEN PEOPLE',
	'k0f544d68' => 'SEARCH',
	'k113470e0' => 'The history, forty minutes, in your own words.',
	'k11b6645b' => 'Each letter holds three things. One symptom is explained, in the same plain language we use in the room, without a promise about what it means for you. One question from a patient is answered, with the name removed and the details changed. Clinic notes follow, the practical kind: holiday hours, a change to the Wednesday evening clinic, a reminder that Sunday and public holidays are closed. The letter began in 2021, in the same year as the headache programme. It is not a digest of research headlines, and it does not sell a test. If a fee is mentioned, it is one of the seven on the fee list, stated the same way.',
	'k121d96de' => 'NURSE SPECIALIST',
	'k1346832d' => 'FINDING US',
	'k13cbf395' => 'A first consultation is €180. The hour is split into forty minutes of history, twenty minutes of examination by hand, and a written plan within five working days, with a copy to your GP. A follow-up consultation is €95 and lasts thirty minutes. A telephone follow-up is €45 and lasts fifteen minutes, for a question that does not need you in the room. A second-opinion review of existing scans and letters is €140. There is no visit. You receive a written reply within ten working days.',
	'k13e9603b' => 'hello@hisagi-neurology.example',
	'k14777b7c' => 'IMAGING',
	'k14e02650' => 'Phone 010 482 0116',
	'k158949e8' => 'Pay by card or bank transfer on the day, except for the second-opinion review, which is paid when the papers are accepted.',
	'k1629eb4b' => 'Night-time numbness in the fingers can come from the nerve at the wrist. A nerve conduction study takes about 45 minutes and can confirm carpal tunnel syndrome. When that is the finding, we refer to a hand surgeon and write down why no brain scan is needed.',
	'k1788caea' => 'A cup that shook',
	'k17ddc0b9' => '15 min',
	'k18075a3e' => 'A day at the clinic',
	'k183da060' => 'The Case Letter is a short note from Hisagi Neurology, sent on the first Tuesday of each month. It takes about four minutes to read, and it carries no advertising.',
	'k18c24a3d' => 'You sit, you stand, you walk a short distance, and we say what we are testing as we go. The point is a finding you can understand, written down the same day in the notes, not a score that only the clinic can read.',
	'k1d9e8d55' => 'EMERGENCY',
	'k1e57009e' => 'Sudden face droop, arm weakness or speech trouble',
	'k1e879ce4' => 'Dr Saskia Lindqvist is the clinical neurophysiologist. She reports the routine EEG and the nerve conduction studies done in the room added in 2016. A study is booked when the consultation has already posed a question the traces can answer, such as a numb hand at night or a spell that may be a seizure. She does not see every first visit. When she does report, the finding goes into the same letter as the plan, within five working days, with a copy to the GP. The fee for the test is separate and listed under fees.',
	'k1eccab6f' => 'Scan only if<br>it changes the plan',
	'k207b0f06' => 'Tests and recordings',
	'k208ef949' => 'the headache keeps returning and you want the pattern set down properly.',
	'k22973c96' => 'Cancel free of charge up to forty-eight hours before the appointment. Later than that, the cancellation fee is €40. Receipts are itemised so you can send them to an insurer. We do not bill insurers directly, and we do not fill in an insurer\'s portal. Pay by card or by bank transfer on the day of the visit. If you are unsure which fee applies, ask before you book. The phone line is Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30, on 010 482 0116, or write to hello@hisagi-neurology.example. The booking card on this site shows the first visit only: sixty minutes, €180.',
	'k252ceaa5' => 'A scan is a picture of structure. It does not say when a shake began, whether a cup makes it worse, or what you fear it means. That history is the longest part of the first hour, and it comes before any test is discussed.',
	'k255b0389' => 'Receipts are itemised for insurers. We do not bill insurers directly.',
	'k25d712bd' => 'Case meeting, daily',
	'k2664f03a' => 'ADDRESS',
	'k2bba21c5' => 'a seizure is happening now, if it is the first and recovery is not prompt, or if it comes with sudden weakness, face droop, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life. Do not use the booking form for an event in progress.',
	'k2d1e5784' => 'Numbness and tingling may sit in the fingers at night, travel up an arm, or appear in the feet. The pattern — which fingers, which time of night, whether shaking the hand out helps — often points to a nerve in the wrist or to something that needs a wider look.',
	'k2dd531f2' => 'Numbness, tingling, and a hand that sleeps',
	'k2e301009' => 'A cup held in both hands.',
	'k2f53d92e' => 'TESTS DONE HERE',
	'k305f46d5' => 'Name and details changed. Every case is different; this is one person\'s account.',
	'k30ad978d' => 'A written plan within five working days, with a copy to your GP.',
	'k31f6064b' => 'Most people who come to Linden Row have already searched the symptom and left more worried. We start again, in plain words, and write down what we heard. If a scan is not needed, we say so, and we say why.',
	'k331804c8' => 'Blood tests, when needed, go through your GP. A scan is a tool with a job. It is not the visit, and it is not a reassurance we offer by default.',
	'k34e4d10b' => 'Second-opinion review',
	'k3519d514' => 'Ground',
	'k35253172' => 'BEFORE',
	'k36098a02' => 'We use a reflex hammer, a tuning fork, and a pen and paper.',
	'k36b15eaf' => 'BY PHONE OR BY FORM',
	'k381bcff7' => 'SYMPTOM 04',
	'k38c698a5' => 'A headache that keeps returning',
	'k38c72fdc' => 'You book by phone or the form. A short questionnaire arrives three working days before.',
	'k3a1e607f' => 'A first visit is sixty minutes: forty for the history, twenty for an examination by hand, and a written plan within five working days. Three principles hold the hour together.',
	'k3b5d8aee' => 'Marta Kowalczyk is the patient coordinator. She answers the phone line, Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30, on 010 482 0116, and she handles bookings made through the form. First appointments are usually offered within three weeks. She sends the short questionnaire three working days before the visit and tells you what to bring: a GP letter if you have one, a medication list, previous scans on a disc or a link, and, if you like, someone who knows you well. Email for the clinic is hello@hisagi-neurology.example. She would rather hear the symptom in your own words than a diagnosis you have guessed.',
	'k3c383a08' => '40 min recording, with report',
	'k3cbe8173' => '30 min',
	'k3dbae2c6' => 'JOURNAL',
	'k3e657b45' => 'About the clinic →',
	'k3eebb26a' => 'CLINICAL NEUROPHYSIOLOGIST',
	'k3f18e8bf' => 'Priya Natarajan',
	'k40a0b409' => 'Dr Kofi Mensah-Hart is a consultant neurologist. His work in the clinic is headache and epilepsy. People with a recurring headache, a blackout, or a possible seizure are often booked with him, including those entering the headache programme. He takes the same first-visit shape as the rest of the clinic: forty minutes of history, twenty minutes of examination, and a written plan within five working days. On Wednesday he is part of the evening clinic, which runs from 11:00 to 19:30. Families are welcome when the person wants them in the room, especially after a first blackout.',
	'k42958ac0' => 'Headache, epilepsy',
	'k42a74b2e' => 'WHAT BRINGS PEOPLE IN',
	'k42e98046' => 'The Case Letter arrives on the first Tuesday of each month. One symptom is explained in about four minutes of reading, and there is no advertising.',
	'k43384f5e' => 'begins with a conversation.',
	'k439e299d' => 'WHY WE TALK FIRST',
	'k44c3c180' => 'FEES',
	'k451a2367' => 'NEUROPHYSIOLOGY TECHNOLOGIST',
	'k45b73ef4' => 'SUBSCRIBE',
	'k45e85c08' => 'you or someone close to you has noticed a change that is persisting, or if a GP has asked for a neurology view.',
	'k461e64e4' => 'Three cases, in full →',
	'k4643645b' => 'ONCE A MONTH',
	'k472792df' => 'WHO IT IS FOR',
	'k47559fb8' => 'NEXT',
	'k4a957a55' => 'Three people agreed to have their stories told with the names changed. Every case is different. Nothing here is a promised result.',
	'k4bfbeb76' => 'First visit + 2 follow-ups + diary review over 12 weeks',
	'k4c27518c' => 'Routine EEG',
	'k4eb3f96b' => 'THE JOURNAL',
	'k4f94e518' => 'The history comes first and takes the longest part of the hour.',
	'k4fa1cdcb' => 'THE PEOPLE',
	'k50201515' => 'numbness arrives suddenly with weakness, face droop, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life. Night-time tingling that has built over weeks is the kind of story we sit down with. A sudden change is not.',
	'k5044ca69' => '2nd floor. Tram line 4 to the Linden Row stop, then 2 minutes on foot. A lift serves the 2nd floor, the entrance is step-free, and two accessible parking bays sit in the courtyard.',
	'k50a94993' => 'A nerve conduction study of the arms or the legs is €240. It takes about forty-five minutes and includes the report. A routine EEG is €210. The recording is forty minutes and the report is included. The headache programme is €360. It covers the first visit, two follow-ups and a diary review over twelve weeks. Tests are booked after a consultation has posed a question, not as a package added at the door. The report from either test is ready within five working days. Saturday, 09:00 to 13:00, is limited to follow-ups and tests.',
	'k54d1bb21' => 'The address may have changed. Try the menu above, or go back to the <a href="/">home page</a>.',
	'k553ea7d8' => 'A nerve conduction study is about forty-five minutes. An EEG recording is forty minutes. The report follows within five working days, in the same letter cycle as a first-visit plan. Fees sit on the fee list in full: €240 for nerve conduction of the arms or legs with report, €210 for a routine EEG with report. Saturday morning, 09:00 to 13:00, is when many of these tests are booked, alongside follow-ups.',
	'k55b6c7c5' => 'Changes in memory worry the person and, just as often, the family who books with them. We want concrete examples: names, appointments, routes, and whether the change is slow or stepped. Mood, sleep and medicines belong in the same conversation.',
	'k5658a339' => 'Dr Saskia Lindqvist',
	'k56f35b64' => 'THREE<br>PRINCIPLES',
	'k58199491' => '45 min<br>nerve conduction',
	'k5a11c781' => 'THE FEE LIST',
	'k5a455a61' => 'Strength',
	'k5a62f11f' => 'Marta Kowalczyk',
	'k5ab9376a' => 'HOURS',
	'k5ba5b6c5' => 'EEG, nerve conduction',
	'k5dadebd7' => 'Bring a GP letter if you have one, a list of your medicines, and any previous scans on a disc or as a link we can open. Bring someone who knows you well, if you like, especially if the symptom is a blackout, a change in memory, or a shake you do not fully see yourself. Wear clothes that let us examine arms and legs without a struggle. For a nerve conduction study or an EEG, the appointment note repeats the preparation: clean hair without product for an EEG, and a word beforehand about any implanted device. The address again: 2nd floor, 14 Linden Row, Westmere.',
	'k6378c0ff' => 'Amara, 51, woke with numb fingers and shook her hand over the side of the bed. The history suggested a nerve at the wrist more than a problem in the brain. A nerve conduction study, about forty-five minutes, fee €240, confirmed carpal tunnel syndrome. She was referred to a hand surgeon. No brain scan was needed, and the letter said why: the question had already been answered by the examination and the study.',
	'k6507419f' => '60 min: 40 min history, 20 min examination, written plan',
	'k65ccab00' => 'PRACTICE MANAGER',
	'k66967b9d' => 'What changed was the plan — a surgical opinion, a note to her GP, and a clear statement that imaging of the head was not the next step. Her name is changed. A night-time numbness that proves to be carpal tunnel in one person is still a story we test, not a label we apply at the door.',
	'k673acbbd' => 'Dr Kofi Mensah-Hart',
	'k6851455f' => 'Adults come to Hisagi Neurology with a new or unexplained neurological symptom, referred by a GP or booking themselves. Families of older patients often come with them.',
	'k693f9511' => 'SYMPTOM 01',
	'k6a7e7316' => 'Hours',
	'k6a980d0d' => 'THE ROUTINE',
	'k6a9d397f' => 'Call emergency services if',
	'k6b2b5614' => 'Journal',
	'k6c47e2be' => 'Numb fingers at night',
	'k6d09dfbd' => 'dizziness comes with sudden weakness, a drooping face, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life. A single violent spinning attack with those signs is an emergency, not a booking.',
	'k6deff228' => 'CASE 03',
	'k7069d15b' => 'Take tram line 4 to the stop called Linden Row. The walk from the stop to 14 Linden Row is two minutes, on a quiet street. The clinic is on the second floor. A lift runs from the entrance to that floor, and the route is step-free. Two accessible parking bays sit in the courtyard. If you use one, allow the same two minutes from the bay to the lift. The waiting room is kept quiet. Come to the glass door at the pale stone front.',
	'k7100b4cf' => 'There is no need to arrive long before your time. The consulting hour starts when you are in the room, and the list is built around that hour.',
	'k718b2106' => 'SYMPTOM 02',
	'k71f01f32' => 'ARCHIVE',
	'k73cdb0d3' => 'Tram line 4, stop Linden Row, 2 minutes\' walk. Lift to the 2nd floor, step-free.',
	'k73d34188' => 'The first visit in four steps',
	'k73d49a1d' => 'Seven people run Hisagi Neurology. The day begins at 08:00 with a case meeting, before the first patient at 08:30.',
	'k76f68dbf' => 'FOUNDER · CONSULTANT NEUROLOGIST',
	'k77c5ed46' => 'Examine by hand',
	'k780625a7' => 'THREE CASES',
	'k791e417a' => '60 min<br>first visit',
	'k79b9be96' => 'the feeling is new, keeps you awake, or is spreading.',
	'k79c6e652' => 'Ruth\'s hands shook around a teacup. She was 64, a retired teacher, and she was afraid the tremor meant Parkinson\'s. The blur in the cup was worse when she reached for it.',
	'k7b35ee2e' => 'Three symptoms we see every week',
	'k7b4133dd' => 'What to send',
	'k7c0705a6' => 'Report<br>in 5 working days',
	'k7c3d8640' => 'Movement disorders, tremor',
	'k7c7c3cc4' => 'Two tests are done in the clinic: a nerve conduction study and a routine EEG. A scan is arranged only when the pictures would change the plan.',
	'k7d44cffd' => 'One symptom explained, once a month',
	'k7d89b8ab' => 'SYMPTOM 03',
	'k7e0cfd21' => 'Ruth, 64, is a retired teacher. She came because her teacup shook and she was afraid the cause was Parkinson\'s. The tremor showed when she reached and poured, not when the hand was at rest. On paper, the spiral and the steadiness of the line, read with a family history of similar shaking, pointed to essential tremor. No scan was ordered. The plan was written with her GP: what the finding meant, what to watch, and what would make us look again.',
	'k7e1f75ac' => 'Rooms, lists and letters',
	'k8007ee08' => 'Listen first.<br>Scan later.',
	'k8115abad' => 'When it arrives',
	'k81a5c389' => 'WHAT THESE ACCOUNTS ARE FOR',
	'k826f76fa' => 'A scan can show structure. It cannot say how a symptom began, what changes it, or what you fear it means. That is why the first hour here is a conversation. Dr Ines Halloran founded Hisagi Neurology in 2012 at 14 Linden Row so the history would come before any machine. You describe the symptom in your own words. We then examine you by hand, with a reflex hammer, a tuning fork, and a pen and paper.',
	'k835a39d8' => 'TEST 01',
	'k8364d774' => 'The work was a history, an examination by hand, and a letter. The tools on the desk have not changed: a reflex hammer, a tuning fork, and pen and paper. The room around them grew only when a new kind of question needed a place to be answered.',
	'k8670a113' => 'The headache programme began, and with it The Case Letter, a short monthly note that explains one symptom.',
	'k88470687' => 'You book by phone or the form, and a short questionnaire arrives three working days before the visit. The visit itself is a history of forty minutes in your own words, then an examination of twenty minutes by hand: reflexes, strength, sensation, coordination and gait. A written plan follows within five working days, with a copy to your GP. The first consultation is sixty minutes and costs €180. First appointments are usually offered within three weeks. If the symptom is sudden face droop, arm weakness, speech trouble, sudden weakness, or the worst headache of your life, do not book. Call emergency services.',
	'k88632f49' => 'PRINCIPLE 01',
	'k8881e6dd' => 'Hisagi is a small neurology clinic in Westmere. We take an hour to hear your symptom, examine you by hand, and explain what we found before any scan is ordered.',
	'k88e18ea0' => 'All fees →',
	'k89bb7829' => 'GETTING HERE',
	'k89c752b7' => 'Second floor, Linden Row',
	'k8ba56d98' => 'A routine EEG records the electrical pattern of the brain from a soft cap of electrodes. You sit or recline in a quiet room with your eyes closed for part of the recording. The technologist fits the cap and may ask you to breathe more deeply for a short interval, or to watch a light. The recording itself takes forty minutes. The fee is €210, with the report.',
	'k8c265388' => 'Getting here',
	'k8cb73c2b' => 'The Case Letter goes out on the first Tuesday of each month. Set aside about four minutes. There is no advertising and no sequence you have to have read before. You can subscribe on this page. The form asks for an email address. If the form hands you to your own email app, you are not subscribed until you send the message to hello@hisagi-neurology.example. You can stop whenever you write and ask. The letter is one note a month, not a thread of reminders. Back copies are not required reading before a visit. The visit still starts with your symptom, not with an essay.',
	'k8cb9b5a3' => 'The day starts at 08:00 with a case meeting. The clinicians sit with the notes from the day before and agree who needs a longer look. First patients are seen at 08:30. Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday run until 17:30. Wednesday is the evening clinic, from 11:00 to 19:30, for people who cannot come in the daytime. Saturday, 09:00 to 13:00, is for follow-ups and tests only.',
	'k8d2428cd' => 'the shake is new, getting in the way of eating or writing, or unexplained after a visit to your GP.',
	'k8e75db1e' => 'BOOK A CONSULTATION',
	'k8fab0f27' => 'The examination takes about twenty minutes and is done by hand. Reflexes, strength, sensation, coordination and gait are the usual sequence, adjusted to the symptom you came with. The tools are ordinary: a reflex hammer at the knee and elsewhere, a tuning fork for vibration, a pen and paper when a line or a spiral will show more than a sentence. There is no white-coat performance to it.',
	'k90adcbe9' => 'The plan was a gradual reduction of the painkillers, agreed with him and copied to his GP, not a sudden stop and not a new medicine chosen on the first morning. What changed was the morning itself, as the overuse eased. His name is changed. A diary that shows overuse in one person does not mean the next headache has the same cause.',
	'k91d6e9d9' => 'Who the hour is for',
	'k91ee7340' => 'All six symptoms →',
	'k91ee8227' => 'A headache that comes back needs dates, not a guess. We ask how often it arrives, what you take for it, and whether mornings are the worst part. A diary kept over the weeks can show painkiller overuse. When that is the picture, the headache programme runs over 12 weeks.',
	'k93f01e68' => 'Late cancellation (less than 48 hours): €40. Receipts are itemised for insurers. We do not bill insurers directly.',
	'k9599415d' => 'Reflexes',
	'k95f50954' => '60 min<br>one hour',
	'k9612ffdf' => 'We refer for a scan only when the result would change the plan, and we say why in writing. A written plan, with a copy to your GP, follows within five working days. We do not promise an outcome. We set out what we found, and what we suggest next, in plain language.',
	'k96800755' => 'Dr Ines Halloran',
	'k968ea00b' => '14 Linden Row, Westmere',
	'k97c323e8' => 'A report from tests done in the clinic is ready within five working days. Nothing in this is a promise that a test will find a cause. It is a promise to say, in writing, why a test was chosen or why it was not.',
	'k97ed35c3' => 'Ruth came afraid of Parkinson\'s. The tremor appeared when she used her hands, not while they rested, and the spiral drawing together with her family history pointed to essential tremor. We did not order a scan. The plan was written with her GP. After 10 weeks she was writing at the kitchen table, and in her words she writes letters again.',
	'k986cfb74' => 'What a visit costs',
	'k9896300c' => 'THE CONSULTING ROOM',
	'k98d03c25' => 'THE CASE LETTER',
	'k9ce5ac4d' => 'How a first visit works →',
	'k9dd1b9dc' => 'HOW WE EXAMINE',
	'k9e83cf23' => 'Hair should be clean and free of spray or oil so the contacts sit properly. It does not hurt. You leave with the cap off and no recovery time built into the appointment. If you are coming because of a possible seizure, bring a witness account if you have one, written in ordinary words.',
	'k9eaa042a' => 'Dizziness and vertigo are easy to mix up, and the difference matters. Some people feel light-headed on standing. Others feel the room spin, or the ground tilt, for seconds or for hours. We ask what you were doing when it started, whether your hearing changed, and whether you have fallen.',
	'ka0026df7' => 'Tremor at rest',
	'ka2034cbc' => 'A hand that shakes',
	'ka271970e' => 'the headache is recurring, changing, or no longer answered by what your GP has already suggested.',
	'ka273f1bc' => 'What happens next',
	'ka2aa203e' => 'Reflex hammer',
	'ka39a3e0c' => 'PRINCIPLE 02',
	'ka49d13cf' => 'This page is not here',
	'ka5366042' => 'The clinic sees adults with a new or unexplained neurological symptom, whether a GP has referred them or they book directly. Families of older patients are welcome, and often they are the ones who make the call. We are an outpatient clinic by appointment. We do not keep an emergency bay, and the phone line is not monitored as an emergency service outside 08:30 to 12:30 on weekdays. Say which days you can travel. The list runs Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday, 08:30 to 17:30, with a Wednesday evening clinic from 11:00 to 19:30. Saturday morning is for follow-ups and tests, not for a first consultation.',
	'ka578fd21' => 'you have sudden weakness, face droop, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life.',
	'ka5ddb6a0' => 'the spells are repeated, unexplained, or affecting walking and work.',
	'ka770bf70' => 'Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday the clinic is open 08:30 to 17:30. Wednesday is the evening clinic, 11:00 to 19:30. Saturday is 09:00 to 13:00 and is for follow-ups and tests only. Sunday and public holidays are closed. The phone line is shorter than the clinic day: Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30, on 010 482 0116. Clinicians meet at 08:00, before the first patient at 08:30. If you are booked on a Wednesday evening or a Saturday morning, the building is open for that list.',
	'ka78bfe0f' => 'Plan in writing<br>in 5 working days',
	'ka79199e0' => 'Follow-up consultation',
	'ka7b4ebef' => 'SYMPTOM 05',
	'ka7b84286' => 'Book a first consultation if',
	'ka9c250f8' => 'She was writing at her kitchen table with a steadier hand. The tremor had come on action, not at rest. In her words, she writes letters again.',
	'kaa8c72ff' => 'Sun and public holidays',
	'kab7569dc' => 'The room turns, or the ground does',
	'kad2718bf' => 'The clinic opened with two consulting rooms.',
	'kadf51168' => 'THREE PRINCIPLES',
	'kaede2578' => 'Tests and the headache programme',
	'kaef80c06' => 'When we order a scan',
	'kb04536ed' => 'Arms or legs, about 45 min, with report',
	'kb0c790db' => 'These are three of the six problems adults bring to a first consultation. Each can be ordinary or urgent, and the difference is in the detail of how it started.',
	'kb15f2c7a' => 'Most of neurology',
	'kb16806e4' => 'Wed (evening clinic)',
	'kb2e112e1' => 'The letter explains a symptom. It does not diagnose the person reading it. A description of tremor, headache, dizziness, numbness, memory or blackouts is there so the words are familiar before you arrive, not so you can sort yourself into a case. If you develop sudden face droop, arm weakness, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life, call emergency services. Do not wait for the next first Tuesday, and do not send the letter a question that needs an answer tonight. For an appointment, use the phone line, Monday to Friday 08:30 to 12:30, or the booking form. The letter is a reading, not a clinic.',
	'kb352e0a6' => 'Tremor is one of the six symptoms we see every week. Some shaking shows at rest. Some appears when the hand reaches for a cup or draws a line. In the examination we look at line steadiness and pen pressure, often with a spiral drawn on blank paper, and we ask when the shake is there and when it is not. A family history can matter as much as the drawing.',
	'kb415a817' => 'Fingers that go numb at night',
	'kb5578e47' => 'The history comes first and takes the longest part of the hour. Forty minutes is set aside for it, and we would rather you talk in your own words than fit yourself into ours. When the symptom started, what it does through a day, what you have already tried, and what you are afraid of are all part of the examination, even though no instrument is involved yet.',
	'kb63fb8a5' => 'Leila Haddad is the practice manager. She keeps the rooms, the lists and the letters moving so that a plan written in the afternoon still leaves the building. Receipts are itemised for insurers. The clinic does not bill insurers directly. Cancellation is free up to forty-eight hours before the appointment. Later, the fee is €40. She is the person who will tell you, plainly, what a visit costs before you come, and she sits in the 08:00 case meeting when the day\'s list needs a room or a longer slot moved.',
	'kb75c2d08' => 'Daniel, 38, was waking with a headache more mornings than not. The first visit was spent on the pattern rather than on a scan. He kept a diary for six weeks: the hour, what he had taken, and whether the pain eased or simply moved. The diary showed painkiller overuse. He joined the headache programme, which is a first visit, two follow-ups and a diary review over twelve weeks, fee €360.',
	'kb8bc922f' => 'NEUROLOGY CLINIC · WESTMERE',
	'kb8f19884' => 'Seven fees, listed in full',
	'kb8fb0333' => 'A pen on a kitchen table.',
	'kb9cc4efb' => 'First Tuesday of each month, about four minutes to read, no advertising.',
	'kba0abcb8' => 'Fees are listed in full before you book. Receipts are itemised for insurers. We do not bill insurers directly.',
	'kbb205816' => 'Listen before we look',
	'kbc3215bf' => 'the fingers go numb or tingle and the cause is still unexplained.',
	'kbc5c2a0d' => '40 min<br>EEG recording',
	'kbd144156' => 'One room, one hour, one doctor.',
	'kbe704c86' => 'Mon, Tue, Thu, Fri',
	'kbed189f2' => 'the headache is sudden and the worst of your life, or if it comes with face droop, arm weakness, speech trouble, or sudden weakness. Do not wait for a clinic slot for those.',
	'kbf84fff1' => 'CASE 02',
	'kbfdc71f5' => 'Nerve conduction study',
	'kc130fda0' => 'AFTER',
	'kc137b170' => 'Sensation',
	'kc1f4a19b' => 'Headache programme',
	'kc2bb0f72' => 'What is in it',
	'kc324ac62' => 'A tremor may appear when the hand is at rest, or only when it reaches for a cup or a pen. A spiral drawing and the family history often sort this more clearly than a scan on day one. We name the pattern we see.',
	'kc390855d' => 'Headaches every morning',
	'kc6b80a46' => 'Pen and paper',
	'kc70b064f' => 'Telephone follow-up',
	'kc7496f5e' => 'A first visit is priced as one hour of listening and examination, not as a scan. The five fees below are the ones most people meet first.',
	'kc7bce1fb' => 'Tomás Reyes is the neurophysiology technologist. He sets up the nerve conduction study and the routine EEG: electrodes, the stimulator, the soft cap, and the quiet of the room while the recording runs. A nerve conduction study is about forty-five minutes. An EEG recording is forty minutes. He explains each step before he does it, including the brief discomfort of the stimulus and the breathing task in the EEG. Saturday morning, 09:00 to 13:00, is often when tests are done, alongside follow-ups. He works from the plan the neurologist has already written, not from a test ordered at the door.',
	'kc7c2e865' => 'Scan only when the answer would change the plan',
	'kc825339d' => 'Listen · Examine · Explain ·',
	'kc87a0d2e' => 'Wear clothing that lets us reach the forearm or the lower leg, and tell us about a pacemaker or implanted device before the day. You can drive afterwards unless something in your own health says otherwise. The report is part of the fee, not a separate letter you have to request.',
	'kca0f00e9' => 'The examination uses a reflex hammer, a tuning fork, and a pen and paper. A spiral drawing, gait and sensation sit beside the history. You leave knowing a written plan will follow within five working days, with a copy sent to your GP.',
	'kcbeb350d' => 'Recording electrode',
	'kced7679c' => 'First appointments are usually offered within three weeks. Bring a GP letter if you have one, a list of medicines, and any previous scans on a disc or as a link. Bring someone who knows you well, if you like. The phone line for booking is open Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30, on 010 482 0116.',
	'kcee0ab79' => 'WHY WE EXPLAIN FIRST',
	'kcf1c3440' => 'ONE CASE',
	'kd06f85e0' => 'SYMPTOM 06',
	'kd145b637' => 'Priya Natarajan is the nurse specialist for the headache programme. The programme is a first visit, two follow-ups and a diary review over twelve weeks. She helps people keep the diary in a form that can actually be read: time, pain, and what was taken. She is often the person on the phone when a headache plan needs a small adjustment between visits, and she writes the note that goes back to the GP with the diary review. The programme fee is €360. She does not replace the consultation. She keeps the twelve weeks coherent.',
	'kd2aee375' => 'Dr Ines Halloran is the founder and a consultant neurologist. Her clinical work is movement disorders and tremor. She opened the clinic in 2012 at 14 Linden Row with two consulting rooms, wanting the history to take longer than the paperwork. She still leads the 08:00 case meeting and writes the plan when the question is a shake, a change in gait, or a fear of a diagnosis the examination does not support. Patients book with her for a first consultation or a follow-up in the ordinary list. The role is the same hour as every other clinician: listen, examine by hand, and explain before any scan.',
	'kd48bc16b' => 'Cancellation, receipts and paying',
	'kd570658a' => 'THE FIRST VISIT',
	'kd61b67dd' => 'confusion is sudden and paired with weakness, face droop, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life. A slow change is a clinic question. A sudden one is an emergency question.',
	'kd63e7c06' => 'BEFORE YOU COME',
	'kd6b54ba5' => 'A neurophysiology room was added, so nerve conduction studies and routine EEG could be done here rather than sent away on the same day they were decided.',
	'kd71c862a' => 'Stimulator',
	'kd939cc2b' => 'If a scan would not change the plan, we do not order one.',
	'kd9a5438d' => 'Why we explain first',
	'kd9e6735e' => 'PATIENT COORDINATOR',
	'kda508313' => 'Tell us the symptom in your own words, how long it has lasted, your GP\'s name, and your medicines. A guessed diagnosis is less useful than a description of what happens in a day. If you are writing rather than calling, use the form on this page. If the form is not available, write to the clinic at hello@hisagi-neurology.example. That opens your email app.',
	'kdaad7a7a' => 'Arriving on a closed day will find the door shut. Write to hello@hisagi-neurology.example if you are unsure of a public holiday.',
	'kdacfe3da' => 'Book by phone or by the form. First appointments are usually offered within three weeks. The phone line is open Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30.',
	'kdb395bcd' => 'Pen pressure',
	'kdcb09054' => 'TIME AND THE REPORT',
	'kdcb73920' => 'A headache that comes back needs a story: the time of day, what you take for it, and what happens over weeks rather than one bad afternoon. Many people who come here have already tried to manage it alone. A diary, kept in ordinary language, often shows a pattern a single visit cannot.',
	'kdd5702e0' => 'First consultation',
	'kdf235043' => 'Hisagi Neurology opened in 2012 at 14 Linden Row, Westmere, so that a symptom could be explained before a scan was ordered. Dr Ines Halloran still runs the clinic on that idea.',
	'kdf2740ac' => 'Sat (follow-ups and tests only)',
	'ke1ce991f' => 'A nerve conduction study checks how quickly a nerve carries a signal, usually in the arms or the legs. Small surface electrodes rest on the skin. A handheld stimulator gives brief pulses near the nerve, often at the wrist or ankle. The recording feels like a series of sharp taps. It is uncomfortable for a moment and then over. The study takes about forty-five minutes, and the fee is €240, including the report.',
	'ke1f65215' => 'Existing scans and letters, written reply in 10 working days, no visit',
	'ke38583f3' => 'CATEGORY',
	'ke444f739' => 'TAG',
	'ke47654c7' => 'CONSULTANT NEUROLOGIST',
	'ke4b4deb2' => 'OPENING TIMES',
	'ke4fadbe1' => 'PRINCIPLE 03',
	'ke518f8d7' => 'Letters are written the same afternoon, so your GP has the plan while the visit is still fresh. Sunday and public holidays the clinic is closed. The phone line is open Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 12:30.',
	'ke587fa48' => 'We refer to an imaging partner only when the result would change the plan, and we explain why in writing. The clinic does not own a scanner. If pictures are the right next step, the letter says what question they are meant to answer, and a copy goes to your GP with the rest of the plan. Blood tests, when they are needed, are arranged through your GP rather than drawn here.',
	'ke5af09ff' => 'CASE 01',
	'ke5b24420' => 'VISIT',
	'ke64629de' => 'Consultations',
	'ke6ca841e' => 'Families of older patients are welcome in the room when the person wants them there. A short questionnaire arrives three working days before the visit so the hour is not spent on dates you would rather have written down at home. Listening is not a courtesy added on. It is the method.',
	'ke8677eb6' => 'What these accounts are for',
	'ke9d55f63' => 'Notes on symptoms and the examination',
	'kea66a10c' => 'Every case is different, and a good outcome in one of them is not an offer of the same outcome to you. If your symptom is sudden weakness, a drooping face, speech trouble, or the worst headache of your life, call emergency services. Do not look for yourself in these pages and wait.',
	'kec1f9bbd' => 'Blackouts and seizures need a witness if you have one, and a clear account of the minutes before and after. We ask whether there was a warning, a fall, a bitten tongue, confusion afterwards, or a known diagnosis of epilepsy already under another doctor.',
	'kec2632df' => 'Scan only when it changes the plan',
	'kecea1ee8' => 'Letter<br>to your GP',
	'kee3b8ec4' => 'Gait',
	'kf05b2c82' => 'Tomás Reyes',
	'kf07c9188' => 'Tuning fork',
	'kf0cd45ee' => '10 weeks',
	'kf1b12d16' => 'Sudden face droop, arm weakness or speech trouble: call emergency services now. Do not book. The same applies to sudden weakness on one side, trouble speaking or understanding, or the worst headache of your life. These are not symptoms to bring to a routine clinic appointment. Hisagi is an outpatient clinic. We see people by appointment for symptoms that have a history we can sit with. If the change is sudden, the right place is emergency care, today, not a form and not a phone message left for the next morning.',
	'kf1c452e6' => 'TEST 02',
	'kf22acdf5' => 'Phone line, bookings',
	'kf2b5189b' => 'Line steadiness',
	'kf367551e' => 'The examination, twenty minutes, by hand — reflexes, strength, sensation, coordination and gait.',
	'kf44fd767' => 'If a test is not the right tool, we say so at the consultation instead of adding it. Preparation is light, and we repeat it in the appointment note so you are not guessing on the morning.',
	'kf4906d48' => 'THE LAST TWELVE YEARS',
	'kf505138a' => 'We order a scan only when the answer would change the plan, and we say why in writing. Many first visits end with no imaging at all: a diagnosis that rests on the history and the examination, a plan shared with your GP, and a clear note of what would make us think again. When a scan is the right next step, we refer you to an imaging partner and explain, in the letter, what question the pictures are meant to answer.',
	'kf5cd0d65' => 'Blackouts and seizures',
	'kf8043944' => 'Time, and the report',
	'kf8ac853c' => 'Plan your visit →',
	'kf8bfb174' => 'We publish cases so you can see the shape of the work: a history, an examination, sometimes a test done here, a scan only when it would change the plan, and a letter. Ruth had no scan. Daniel had a diary and the headache programme. Amara had a nerve conduction study and a referral on, not a brain scan. Names and details are changed.',
	'kfce0c0ca' => 'What it will not do',
	'kfd3669b1' => 'the shaking is new, unexplained, or getting in the way of eating or writing.',
	'kfe5c8b01' => 'Phone line, Mon–Fri',
	'search_results' => 'Search results for: %s',
);
